message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below. If you use the argument, please also cite the accompanying paper."
title: "What a Quantum Milestone Warrants: Computational Supplement"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kahl"
    given-names: "Peter"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher, Lex et Ratio"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-1616-4843"
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-10-16"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Peter-Kahl/quantum-milestone-warrants"
url: "https://www.lexetratio.com"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Computational supplement to 'What a Quantum Milestone Warrants: Error
  Correction, Evidence and Scaling Decisions' (Lex et Ratio Working Paper
  LXR-2026-QUANT-WQMW-WP). A toy decision model of the
  choice to scale a below-threshold quantum error-correction memory. Three
  scripts: a check that the suppression factor fitted at small code distances
  is blind to rare correlated events that would change the decision, with the
  run length a zero-failure demonstration would need; a preposterior
  value-of-information model comparing candidate experiments (the headline
  metric, counting events, tagging events at one and at two code distances)
  against the value of perfect and of partial perfect information; and
  robustness checks for non-additivity of information, a change in scaling
  beyond the largest distance tested, and misattribution of ordinary failures
  to events. Plus the script for Figure 6.1 and reference outputs. Not a model
  of any real device.
keywords:
  - "quantum error correction"
  - "value of information"
  - "expected value of sample information"
  - "partial expected value of perfect information"
  - "decision analysis"
  - "correlated errors"
  - "surface code"
  - "scaling decisions"
  - "evidence"
